; One executable per module under test; they all share the Support fixtures
; and testables. Nothing here opens a window. Framebuffer.offscreen builds a
; buffer with no streaming texture behind it, and Renderer.draw_frame fills one
; with no SDL call in it, so test_renderer draws whole frames and reads the
; pixels back — as do test_paint and test_font. Only Renderer.render itself,
; which is the upload and the present, is left untested, and there is nothing in
; it but those two calls. Input reads SDL for the keyboard and the mouse, but
; its edges and hold timer are a pure function of two frames and a duration, and
; test_input drives that directly; Binding turns such a frame into a movement
; and touches nothing at all, so test_binding drives that.
;
; The demo's suites live here too, beside the engine's own, because they share
; these fixtures and there is no reason to run them separately by hand. A game
; built on this engine tests itself in its own repo.
;
; Two stanzas rather than one, because the two libraries are two packages and a
; package's suite has to be buildable from that package alone. `dune runtest`
; runs the lot; `-p camlcast @runtest` drops the second stanza and never asks
; for the demo library; `-p camlcast-demo @runtest` drops the first. One stanza
; put camlcast_demo in the engine's test build, which is the same confusion of
; the two that had the demos installing with the engine.
;
; Both stay in this directory. Asset looks one level above the executable, so a
; suite in test/ finds the assets/ that (source_tree ../assets) puts in
; _build/default/; a suite in test/somewhere/ would be a level too deep, and a
; source_tree dependency does not move the tree to meet it.

; Support is a library because two stanzas cannot both claim support.ml, and a
; library of one module named for it exposes that module as itself — so
; `open Support` in all thirty suites reads exactly as it did. No package: an
; unpackaged private library survives either -p build, and a test executable,
; which installs nothing, is allowed to depend on one.

(library
 (name support)
 (modules support)
 (libraries camlcast alcotest))

; The engine's own. The suites that load pictures read them from fixtures/ by
; plain relative path, because dune runs a test with its working directory here
; — so the loaders are tested without going through Asset, and Asset is tested
; without going near SDL: test_asset drives the lookup with a made-up exists and
; opens no file at all.
;
; The modules are named by subtraction so that a suite added to the stanza below
; and forgotten here is dune's "used in several stanzas" error rather than a
; test that quietly joined the wrong package.

(tests
 (names
  test_vec
  test_result_ext
  test_asset
  test_bitmap
  test_paint
  test_renderer
  test_font
  test_plane
  test_sky
  test_image
  test_transform
  test_room
  test_world
  test_ray
  test_player
  test_viewport
  test_color
  test_texture
  test_material
  test_atmosphere
  test_input
  test_binding
  test_key
  test_sight
  test_clock
  test_engine)
 (modules
  :standard
  \
  support
  test_loom
  test_stage
  test_check
  test_debug_map
  test_events
  test_overlay
  test_patterns
  test_pictures
  test_level
  test_demos
  test_menu)
 (package camlcast)
 (deps
  (glob_files fixtures/*))
 (libraries camlcast alcotest support))

; The runtime's own, and a stanza to itself for the same reason loom's dune has
; an empty (libraries) line. A suite sitting in the engine's stanza would link
; camlcast, and could then come to lean on it without anyone noticing — at which
; point the independence is a thing to remember rather than a thing the build
; will not let you break. Support is absent for that reason too: it is built on
; the engine's types, and a host made of strings has no use for a Vec testable.
;
; It belongs to the camlcast package because camlcast.loom does. `-p camlcast
; @runtest` runs it; `-p camlcast-demo @runtest` does not.

(tests
 (names test_loom)
 (modules test_loom)
 (package camlcast)
 (libraries camlcast_loom alcotest qcheck-alcotest))

; The binding's own. This one does link camlcast, because that is the whole of
; what it is testing: that a description assembles into the same world the old
; API builds by hand. Support comes with it for the Vec and float testables — a
; failing comparison should print (3, 2.5) and not a bare false.

(tests
 (names test_stage test_check test_debug_map test_events test_overlay)
 (modules test_stage test_check test_debug_map test_events test_overlay)
 (package camlcast)
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_stage camlcast_loom alcotest support))

; The demos'. Their art comes in through Asset rather than by relative path,
; which is why the whole of assets/ is a dependency: test_demos builds every
; demo's world and one of them — loading — reads files. The other four need
; nothing on disk, but the dependency is on the stanza so that a demo suite
; which grows a disk read later does not have to remember to ask for it.

(tests
 (names test_patterns test_pictures test_level test_demos test_menu)
 (modules test_patterns test_pictures test_level test_demos test_menu)
 (package camlcast-demo)
 (deps
  (source_tree ../assets))
 (libraries camlcast camlcast_demo camlcast_stage alcotest support))
